#!RuleTest
#test CDISC-AD0320 expect=skipped domain=ADSLX
#note "ADSL negative. SUBJECT LEVEL ANALYSIS DATASET is derived from an EXACT dataset name of ADSL, never from a prefix, so ADSLX is not it — the columns then decide, and PARAMCD/AVAL make it a BASIC DATA STRUCTURE, outside this rule's Data_Structures scope. The label is deliberately wrong, so the rule would fire on this fixture if the structure gate ever admitted an ADSL-prefixed name; expect=skipped asserts the non-execution that expect=noViolation would hide."
# Rule:Description: A dataset is named ADSL and the dataset label is not "Subject-Level Analysis Dataset"
dataset ADSLX label="Wrong Label"
col STUDYID type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col USUBJID type=Char label="Unique Subject Identifier"
col PARAMCD type=Char label="Parameter Code"
col AVAL    type=Num  label="Analysis Value"
---
CDISCPILOT01 | 01-701-1015 | HEIGHT | 175
---
